Eisvogel pandoc templates
=========================

These files are copied unchanged from the Eisvogel release `v3.5.1`:

- `eisvogel.latex`
- `eisvogel.beamer`

Upstream: https://github.com/Wandmalfarbe/pandoc-latex-template
License: BSD-3-Clause; see `LICENSE`.
Imported: 2026-08-24
Local modifications: none

Take both files from the same release archive (`Eisvogel-VERSION.tar.gz`),
not from the repository's default branch: `template-multi-file/` there holds
the split source, and the single-file templates only exist once
`tools/release.sh` has spliced the partials together.

Both are pandoc templates written in pandoc's template language, so only
pandoc can expand them.  `ox-latex` builds its preamble from
`org-latex-classes` and a standalone `.tex` has no template stage at all;
neither can consume these files.  Which pandoc formats select which template,
and the variables that go with them, belong in `org/32-org-pandoc.org`.
